1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,500
This is ProfileProof—the real product, including where it can fail.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:23,000
The public application runs on Google Cloud Run and validates, verifies,
normalizes, and adds provenance to professional profile data.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:41,000
The safe sample exercises the deployed API and complete product interface
without exposing anyone's private data.

4
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Raw JSON exposes source mode, limitations, warnings, request ID,
cache state, and the versioned schema.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The production LinkedIn path is browserless and directly calls
reverse-engineered HTTP surfaces.

6
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Invalid URLs fail before any upstream call. Redaction, rate limits,
session expiry, and schema changes remain explicit.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Cloud Run uses an automatically discovered residential worker because
LinkedIn blocks Google data-center egress. The Mac must remain online.

8
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Typed output, honest provenance, graceful failure,
and a real production deployment.
